# OCI 9.2's execute of BEGIN :1 := zz_o9(8, 'out'); END;, :1 an object OUT.
# Captured 2026-11-08 from a client net trace (TRACE_LEVEL_CLIENT 16) of an OCI
# 9.2 program on the 9i bed itself, Oracle 9.2.0.4, x86-64 Linux (OCI_OBJECT
# mode; OCIBindObject of an instance of ZZ_O9, an OBJECT (id NUMBER, name
# VARCHAR2(20)), or of ZZ_T9, a TABLE OF NUMBER). The TTC payload, without the
# packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the |ascii|
# gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
